+**Design Impact, not Requirement Gap.** Compaction BEH004/005/007, SCN004/005/006, REQ004/005/007/012/013 and AC008/013/014/017/018 still govern. Upstream UC001/004, REQ001/003/006/008/011/013 establish normal standalone `@` admission, dormant hosted Agents/Teams, direct child chat, reconnect, retained membership and root Stop. Applying already-approved recovery/Stopped behavior to their native AgentRuns changes no intended outcome. Keep upstream REQ014/AC016 sender identity live and after reopen; no inference for old messages without sender facts. No new scenario IDs/requirements, provider/default/retry policy, input retention lifetime or native cold-history promise.
+
+Forward witness: user adds an Agent/Team in the standalone composer -> admission publishes one dormant hosted instance -> user opens/messages the collaborator -> that native AgentRun reaches ordinary pre-parent or post-response compaction -> user reconnects or terminates the host -> exact child projection/history is inspected. The normal path is **Supported Normal Scenario**; compaction exhaustion and termination during compaction are the existing **Supported Explicit Edge Scenarios**. No manually repeated command-ID premise. `delegate_task` extra copies retain upstream semantics; they are not the normal mention-created instance.
