+E35/source-evidence.json records current source and IR008 evidence. LF001 is an executed **local** production-projector/strict-schema failure on an ordinary dormant child (empty control Pass). DI001.a/b/c consequences are source-derived, not newly executed product proof. The new root owns children, not host; its stream connection can restore a host, whereas GraphQL inspection cannot. Child inactive is not a successful root-Stop receipt: local finish can fail after publishing inactive; host termination is later still. The current web publish mutates retained contexts before activity commit and reads revisions after awaited projections. These are material integration boundaries, not grounds to revive the retired compactor.
