+### Tradeoffs / final classification / escalation
+Intentional child pre-retirement is a small, explicit command/view ordering choice; it reuses the proven Org approach instead of adding stream-retirement receipts or redefining ROOT_LIFECYCLE. Failure cannot prove which unseen child stopped; preserve uncertainty rather than fabricate partial success. Holding off hydration during Stop is local publication exclusion, not durable input retention. Snapshot revision guards reject concurrent updates rather than silently overwrite them; fresh reads cost another existing read but no generation. No general shutdown SLA or guarantee about other clients racing reactivation is introduced; qualify only exact evidence and available instance identity.
